<newsitem itemid="18089" id="root" date="1996-08-27" xml:lang="en">
<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish Permanent H1 pretax profit up 16.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Irish Permanent H1 pretax profit up 16.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>					  (million punts unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		15.9		   vs 13.8</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	  4.0		    vs 3.5</p>
<p> Pretax		     23.3		   vs 19.9</p>
<p> Total income	     57.2		   vs 52.0</p>
<p> Net interest income    48.5		   vs 44.5</p>
<p> Tax charge		  7.0		    vs 5.9</p>
<p> Net taxed		  16.3		   vs 14.1</p>
<p> Registration date October 23, 1996</p>
<p> Pay date	    October 24, 1996</p>
<p>NOTE - Irish Permanent Plc said the strong performance in the first half was achieved against a background of increased competition within its core markets.</p>
<p>-- Dublin newsroom 353 1 660 3377</p>
</text>
